00:12:02.588 --> 00:12:09.613
smuggling, which This type of request
magning was thought to be impossible

00:12:09.623 --> 00:12:14.523
because it doesn't really make sense
because if you're familiar with, um, with

00:12:14.533 --> 00:12:18.673
request smuggling, you have basically
two headers to describe the length

00:12:18.713 --> 00:12:22.713
of the body of the request, which is
content length and the transfer encoding.

00:12:23.693 --> 00:12:27.463
Content length is the one we all know
because it's in almost every single

00:12:27.463 --> 00:12:29.733
request with a body and transfer encoding.

00:12:29.803 --> 00:12:34.963
Usually from one sent from
the client is not used, but is

00:12:34.963 --> 00:12:36.283
the one that has the priority.

00:12:36.283 --> 00:12:38.973
So request smuggling happens
with when this prior route.

00:12:39.288 --> 00:12:41.938
prioritization is done incorrectly.

00:12:43.488 --> 00:12:47.558
So usually you will have the transfer
and coding head and slightly modified

00:12:47.838 --> 00:12:51.258
so that one component, let's say you're
reverse, you have reverse proxy in

00:12:51.258 --> 00:12:54.808
the server or from your perspective,
first reverse proxy, then the server.

00:12:55.498 --> 00:13:00.138
And it happens when one component does
not see the transfer and coding header.

00:13:00.378 --> 00:13:04.158
So it chooses the content next header,
and the other component sees both.

00:13:04.368 --> 00:13:08.498
So it prioritizes the transfer and
coding header, which was first ignored.

00:13:09.098 --> 00:13:10.598
So this is the normal situation.

00:13:11.318 --> 00:13:18.358
So the TL zero was thought to be
impossible because it works the

00:13:18.358 --> 00:13:22.048
way that for, to the first, uh,
component to the reverse proxy.

00:13:22.048 --> 00:13:26.448
You send the transfer and coding header
and you hope for it to be somehow

00:13:26.448 --> 00:13:27.978
dropped by the second component.

00:13:28.348 --> 00:13:30.748
Which normally shouldn't happen
because it's the one with the

00:13:30.758 --> 00:13:33.778
priority, but It did work.

00:13:34.848 --> 00:13:38.448
Um, I think what happened here,
if I were to guess, is that

00:13:38.458 --> 00:13:40.148
first, it's an options request.

00:13:40.218 --> 00:13:43.938
So maybe this code base was
not examined as thoroughly.

00:13:44.598 --> 00:13:47.768
And then there's no content
length in this request at all.

00:13:47.948 --> 00:13:54.578
So my guess would be that there was some
code that said, if there is no content

00:13:54.578 --> 00:13:59.533
length header, then there's Treat the
content length as zero so it would treat

00:13:59.553 --> 00:14:04.673
the body as zero even though there was
transfer encoding header and That's how

00:14:04.683 --> 00:14:10.553
the smuggling happened and this happened
in the Google Um, Google cloud proxy.

